    "meaning": "as; than; when (once, in the past)",
    "shortDefinition": "As, than, or when (for one past event)."
  },
  "intro": {
    "title": "Three jobs for one little word",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Als does three different jobs. It means 'as' for a role: Ich arbeite als Kellner. It means 'than' in comparisons: Er ist älter als ich. And it means 'when' for a single event in the past: Als ich ein Kind war, …",
      "That last one fights with wenn. The rule: one time in the past → als. Every time, or in the present and future → wenn."
    ]
  },
